# 2026-11-09 (r90, wall-86 fix): r89 pinned the SIGSEGV to launchd consuming a
# poisoned plain-rebase slot in a cache subcache page, and the bytes are not
# derivable from any donor bytes (knife-a: decompressed linkedit scan, data
# subcache transforms, on-flash donor-exact). This round's recon found the
# delivery topology: iOS26 dyld maps each cache subcache with kernel page-in
# linking (map_with_linking_np), and on failure falls back to "linking
# in-process" - dyld applies the chained fixups itself (its log line
# "__map_with_linking_np(subcache %d) failed, falling back to linking
# in-process", decoded from the 24A446 dyld binary). Our kernel rejects the
# call because map_with_linking_np only accepts mwli_page_size == PAGE_SIZE
# (4 KiB) while the arm64e 24A446 cache bakes 16 KiB fixup pages, and the
# dyld pager fixup walkers (pageIndex/end_contents) are PAGE_SIZE-based - so
# this lane alone runs the userspace fallback path that no real hardware ever
# exercises ("some older devs have s/w page size > h/w page size, no need to
# support them"). Sheng's lane accepts 4*PAGE_SIZE and assembles the whole
# 16 KiB fixup page in a kernel buffer (dyld_pager_peek + scratch copy-out),
# which is the configuration that reached SpringBoard on the same donor.
# These hunks are that section of zzzz-sheng-ipados27-bringup-core.patch
# (vm_dyld_pager.c whole + the map_with_linking_np acceptance hunk), split
# out standalone with the same recipe as sheng-shared-region-sign-gate.patch;
# the sheng-* one-shot printfs are kept deliberately as first-flash evidence
# of which fixup path is live. The dyld_a_key == 0 sign gate mirrors the v5
# slide gate this lane already removed in sheng-shared-region-sign-gate.patch.
